{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790488902,"nonce":"6V17sPdGTwxiYo6FnIfpDpIKDKA=","title":"Python: None-default parameters of instances and Str-or-None narrowing","message":"Left from P-none-narrowing. (1) The fold of `if x is None: x = e` needs every call of the item to pass None (Sig.none_params, closed items only). An instance made for the call sites that omit the argument still keys the parameter as Object (spec_ty(None) = Object), so a function called both with and without the argument keeps the version dynamic; keying such an instance on None needs the IR to carry a None-typed parameter (ir(None) is Unit) or an instance-level none_params. Methods reached dynamically (telco's Decimal.quantize, a dynamic method) never infer their parameters, so `rounding` stays Object there. (2) Str-or-None stays Object; after an `is not None` test (Walker.nonnone / Lowerer.nonnull facts) it could read as Str through a checked unbox. (3) The `if x is None: \u003cleaves\u003e` form (b) versions nothing: the lowering and typer narrow a Num or list-or-None after it, but an Object-typed name stays Object.","files":null}]}